{"team":"NO","col":"#D9BE72","identity":"run-heavy","funnel":"run-funnel","plays_pg":61.5,"adot":8.1,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Bleed the Clock</h2><p>There's no bell-cow to bank on \u2014 the lead back sees just <strong>51%</strong> of carries (league ~59%), a committee that caps any one back's ceiling and makes their rushing props matchup- and script-dependent.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>They spread the ball as much as anyone \u2014 the WR1 commands only <strong>19%</strong> of targets (league ~23%). Volume is democratic here, which suppresses any single receiver's ceiling but props up the TE and secondary options.</p><p>They lean on tempo \u2014 a 16% no-huddle rate (league ~11%) that inflates snap counts and everyone's volume.</p><p>By the numbers it's a struggling unit \u2014 a 41% success rate (below the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Their red-zone identity is <strong>run-first</strong> (48% pass), funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>Travis Etienne</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 Soft on the Ground</h2><p>They surrender <strong>132 rushing</strong> and <strong>224 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). The run moves against them \u2014 <strong>target opposing RB1s</strong>.</p><p>They lock down opposing WR1s \u2014 just 51 rec yds/game (vs ~58); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They leak <strong>RB rushing TDs</strong> (0.68/game vs ~0.46) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>They leak <strong>WR1 receiving TDs</strong> (0.47/game vs ~0.38) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: back <strong>Travis Etienne</strong>'s rushing volume in favored/positive scripts; <strong>opposing RB1s</strong> smash on the ground and at the goal line.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Tyler Shough","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":19,